doc:FactsDesignDetailDnd None:has_text_value "acoustic data gathered using a standard cell phone; acoustic emissions documented at pressure reductions 0-390 kPa; data analyzed using MATLAB 'Audio' and 'DSP' toolboxes; three tendencies related to flow rate and pressure decrease identified; cavitation commencement particularly within 50-80 kPa; 'flatness' characteristic correlated with cavitation levels and device efficacy; suitable for real-time detection and broadly applicable across cavitation systems" .
